1
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:24,668
HWANG DAESIK

2
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:25,686
For crying out loud.

3
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:29,565
Not a single one of those so-called
government ministers ever comes prepared.

4
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:30,983
I swear.

5
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:34,112
They should have everything ready
before I even say a word.

6
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:37,824
Advisor Jang, what brings you here
at the crack of dawn?

7
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:42,161
General, you're attending
the ten o'clock meeting today, right?

8
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:44,121
Yeah.  Oh, God.

9
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:46,040
I don't know
if it's the season,

10
00:02:46,041 --> 00:02:47,751
but I feel like crap.

11
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:50,879
So, um, what about the meeting?

12
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:54,465
Well, since you're
a little under the weather,

13
00:02:54,466 --> 00:02:56,259
why don't you take break on this one?

14
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:59,221
What? You think I should cancel it?

15
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:05,102
Oh, no. Today's meeting…

16
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,355
must start on schedule.

17
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:11,149
At 10:00 a.m. sharp.

18
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:19,449
Is this C-4?

19
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:50,480
-  Miss Oh.
- Yes?

20
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,542
Has Captain Min Jonghwan come in yet?

21
00:04:12,461 --> 00:04:14,671
No, haven't seen him today.

22
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:18,091
Miss Oh.

23
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,970
I'm gonna tell you something
very important.

24
00:04:23,138 --> 00:04:24,389
Listen carefully.

25
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,017
Min is gonna have…

26
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:29,936
a bomb with him today.

27
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:33,606
A… A bomb? Really?

28
00:04:52,876 --> 00:04:54,503
Min has arrived for the meeting.

29
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:58,715
Let's move, then.

30
00:05:14,523 --> 00:05:15,524
Miss Oh.

31
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:19,778
Let's keep this strictly
between the two of us…

32
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:23,114
until we've apprehended Baek Kitae.

33
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:29,204
Do you know where General Hwang is?

34
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:32,498
Present arms!

35
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:34,042
Yes, sir!

36
00:05:54,813 --> 00:05:56,815
HWANG DAESIK

37
00:06:04,573 --> 00:06:06,283
Min just arrived in the office.

38
00:06:10,579 --> 00:06:11,997
What about Colonel Baek?

39
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:14,749
I didn't see him around earlier.

40
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,068
Are you looking
for something, ma'am?

41
00:06:44,362 --> 00:06:45,739
Where are you going?

42
00:07:06,509 --> 00:07:09,179
Captain Min.

43
00:07:12,682 --> 00:07:14,059
Captain, hey.

44
00:07:14,643 --> 00:07:16,144
Ah. Yes, sir.

45
00:07:16,895 --> 00:07:20,398
So, did you manage
to get what I asked you for?

46
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:22,942
Oh, yes, sir. I have it here.

47
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:28,823
PERSONAL RECORD

48
00:07:34,746 --> 00:07:37,540
Thank you. New briefcase, huh?

49
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,127
Uh, yeah. Someone gave it to me.

50
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:47,967
Oh, nice.
American-made.

51
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:51,345
How 'bout that. Made in the USA.

52
00:07:51,346 --> 00:07:53,431
- How do you open this thing?
- Uh, sorry.

53
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:57,518
I have a meeting soon.

54
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:58,602
Excuse me.

55
00:07:58,603 --> 00:07:59,813
Have a good day, sir.

56
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:57,954
Captain Min.

57
00:08:58,747 --> 00:08:59,748
Yes, sir.

58
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:01,541
You gonna grab a seat?

59
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:06,671
I was gonna have a smoke
before the meeting.

60
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:12,302
All right.

61
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,083
When you're ready,

62
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:47,461
set the combination lock
on the left side of the briefcase

63
00:09:47,462 --> 00:09:49,714
to three, eight, six.

64
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:58,515
Once you do, the circuit will activate,

65
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:02,602
and it will automatically arm
the detonator connected to the lock.

66
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:06,731
After exactly ten minutes,
the bomb will go off.

67
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:10,734
The lethal blast radius
is about 20 meters,

68
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:13,237
so leave it by your seat
and get out of there.

69
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:49,106
-  Colonel Ahn.
- Yes, sir.

70
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:51,317
From now on,
let's schedule these in the afternoon.

71
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:54,111
I haven't even had breakfast yet.

72
00:10:54,112 --> 00:10:55,113
Understood, sir.

73
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:57,949
Where's the commander?

74
00:10:58,867 --> 00:10:59,909
Don't worry, he's coming.

75
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,039
Captain Min.

76
00:11:47,624 --> 00:11:48,625
Yes, sir?

77
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:59,302
The meeting is gonna start soon.

78
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:01,971
Where are you going?

79
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,935
Um, I was going to go get the report.

80
00:12:19,739 --> 00:12:22,574
Stop! Don't move, you bastard!

81
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:29,999
Everyone, stay where you are.

82
00:12:40,093 --> 00:12:41,176
Colonel Ahn.

83
00:12:46,224 --> 00:12:47,683
Get everybody out.

84
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:49,059
Are we evacuating?

85
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:51,979
Everybody needs to leave the room now!
It's an emergency. Get out!

86
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,439
- Get out of here now.
-  What the hell is going on?

87
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:57,735
I'll explain later, sir. Hey, make sure
the Chief of Staff gets out. Hurry!

88
00:12:58,444 --> 00:13:00,988
- Move it, let's go!
-  Come on, hurry.

89
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:02,823
Get him out of here now!

90
00:13:02,824 --> 00:13:04,574
- Move it!
-  Hey…

91
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:06,160
Geez.

92
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:09,289
You too, Ahn.

93
00:13:09,998 --> 00:13:11,040
Yeah.

94
00:13:13,835 --> 00:13:14,961
And you, Miss Oh.

95
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:16,587
Let's go, asshole.

96
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:18,798
Come on.

97
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:21,466
Get out.

98
00:14:06,137 --> 00:14:08,681
I'm not seeing a red wire.

99
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:33,200
You said he was
supposed to be in this car!

100
00:16:33,201 --> 00:16:34,327
Sir. Wait.

101
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:40,917
- Sir! We've got JIH vehicles incoming.
- Kihyun.

102
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:44,336
Director Baek, it's a trap, sir.

103
00:16:44,337 --> 00:16:45,754
- We have to go right now.
- Kihyun.

104
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:47,798
What are you doing here? Come on, Kihyun.

105
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:50,050
- Stop, wait. Kihyun!
- We have to go.

106
00:16:50,051 --> 00:16:52,719
Kihyun, you're all right.
Hey, Kihyun. Get off me, asshole.

107
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,055
- Hey, Kihyun! Wake up!
-  Sir, we have to go.

108
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:09,403
-  We have to go.
- Kihyun, wake up! Kihyun!

109
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:11,572
Wake up!

110
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:14,991
- Kihyun! Wake up, damn it!
-  Keep moving.

111
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:17,160
- Hey, cover him!
-  Kiyhun! Kihyun, please!

112
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:18,745
They're coming.
Sir, we have to go now.

113
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:20,247
- Sir, please.
- Wake up, for God's sake!

114
00:17:20,248 --> 00:17:23,709
- Get the hell off me! Kihyun!
-  Cover him, you idiots! Hey!

115
00:17:24,335 --> 00:17:26,503
- Get in the car, sir. Shut the door.
- Kihyun, no!

116
00:17:46,107 --> 00:17:48,149
You little rat.

117
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:49,943
Damn you.

118
00:17:49,944 --> 00:17:52,196
Oh. Oh.

119
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,788
Oh, shit. I'm so screwed.

120
00:18:08,713 --> 00:18:09,714
General.

121
00:18:12,842 --> 00:18:14,885
Did you get him? Baek Kitae?

122
00:18:16,012 --> 00:18:17,013
He escaped.

123
00:18:21,601 --> 00:18:23,436
It'd be a lot better for us…

124
00:18:24,437 --> 00:18:26,230
if that asshole was just dead.

125
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:32,153
Long as he's breathing, he's a liability.

126
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:34,947
Yes, sir. Copy that.

127
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:36,532
Goddamn.

128
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,160
If Jang hadn't told me,

129
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,870
I would've wound up dead, right?

130
00:18:41,871 --> 00:18:44,498
Baek Kitae, that bastard.
I don't believe it!

131
00:18:47,043 --> 00:18:48,418
All right. I'm gonna…

132
00:18:48,419 --> 00:18:50,795
I'm gonna head over
to the safe house for now.

133
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:52,756
Stay put and make sure everything's okay.

134
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:54,382
- Got it?
-  I'll get the car ready, sir.

135
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:56,009
-  Yeah, let's go.
- Hang on, wait a minute.

136
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:57,386
What?

137
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:01,974
I think that Baek Kihyun
should be sent there before you.

138
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:03,767
Baek Kihyun?

139
00:19:03,768 --> 00:19:04,769
Him first?

140
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:07,354
Trust me on this, General.

141
00:19:07,355 --> 00:19:10,024
Baek Kitae's dangled bait
in front of me before.

142
00:19:11,192 --> 00:19:13,319
And if you decide to take it,
you'll end up caught.

143
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,696
What? B-Bait?

144
00:19:16,739 --> 00:19:17,865
Yes.

145
00:19:18,783 --> 00:19:20,868
So what if this bomb is some kind of bait?

146
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,996
What do you mean, it's bait?

147
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,959
You think…

148
00:19:29,627 --> 00:19:31,545
he'll ambush me
on the way to the safe house?

149
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,967
Okay. So then…

150
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:40,054
Now what? What do you recommend?

151
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:45,475
I think you should just sit tight

152
00:19:45,476 --> 00:19:49,688
and enjoy a nice, big bowl
of jjajangmyeon, sir.

153
00:19:49,689 --> 00:19:50,981
That's all you have to do.

154
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:53,901
What?

155
00:19:55,403 --> 00:19:57,113
- Drop your head.
- Yes, sir.

156
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:01,117
Baek Kitae is a fucking bastard!

157
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:05,621
That sly little asshole is going down.

158
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,291
DIRECTOR BAEK KITAE

159
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,210
So Baek Kitae…

160
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:16,005
…made an attack
on Hwang Daesik's armored car?

161
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:17,633
Yes, sir.

162
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:21,637
And Hwang was nowhere to be found, right?

163
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:24,598
- Correct, Mr. Pyo.
- Just Baek Kihyun?

164
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:37,861
Jang Geonyoung's pretty clever, huh?

165
00:20:37,862 --> 00:20:40,865
Everyone's plotting. No one's safe.

166
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:44,368
Someone's gonna have to die.

167
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:52,960
It's not gonna be me.

168
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:55,629
It better not be.

169
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:01,885
What is this?

170
00:21:07,850 --> 00:21:08,934
Get him out.

171
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:12,146
Go. It's fine.

172
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:21,238
I was just going to call you.

173
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:24,282
What's going on with Baek Kitae?

174
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:26,326
Where do you think
someone like him would hide?

175
00:21:26,327 --> 00:21:27,411
You lost him?

176
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,664
The KCIA's got a few
major safe houses, doesn't it?

177
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:34,877
I want a detailed map
with all their locations marked right now.

178
00:21:40,508 --> 00:21:42,092
Let's make a deal first.

179
00:21:49,809 --> 00:21:51,227
Baek Kitae is captured…

180
00:21:53,187 --> 00:21:54,438
and this chair is mine.

181
00:22:03,781 --> 00:22:06,575
- Where are the safe hou--
- I want your word on this first.

182
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:10,329
Why don't I…

183
00:22:10,955 --> 00:22:14,082
have these soldiers drag you down
to the basement of the JIH

184
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:15,417
and we can talk there instead?

185
00:22:16,210 --> 00:22:17,920
You like that option better?

186
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,175
Come on, don't do this.

187
00:22:25,928 --> 00:22:27,596
- The safe houses.
- All right, all right.

188
00:22:29,265 --> 00:22:30,432
Give me a sec.

189
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:35,396
The map's in my office.

190
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:38,232
Go with him.

191
00:23:03,257 --> 00:23:04,757
Oh, look at you.

192
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:07,511
My goodness.
What happened, Chief Cheon?

193
00:23:08,012 --> 00:23:10,264
Oh, gosh, you look awful right now.

194
00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:14,518
I haven't heard from you for awhile.
Guess you're a little busy.

195
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:18,689
So what brings you here today, Madam Shin?

196
00:23:21,442 --> 00:23:24,444
Well, you'll be glad to know

197
00:23:24,445 --> 00:23:27,239
that I've been praying
day and night for you, sir.

198
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:31,910
You better be fucking kidding me
with this praying shit.

199
00:23:31,911 --> 00:23:35,039
Hwang is coming.
He's out for blood, don't you get that?

200
00:23:36,457 --> 00:23:39,335
Staring up at the sky and mumbling
isn't gonna solve anything.

201
00:23:41,545 --> 00:23:45,048
They kick the crap out of you
and you're as blockheaded as ever.

202
00:23:45,049 --> 00:23:48,802
You're such a helpless, pathetic man,
but you can't stop running your mouth.

203
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:54,391
That certainly explains
why you're still rotting in this dungeon.

204
00:23:55,976 --> 00:23:57,144
Doesn't it?

205
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:06,362
Are you on drugs?

206
00:24:07,196 --> 00:24:09,573
- What's the matter with you?
- All right.

207
00:24:10,616 --> 00:24:12,701
You listen here, Chief Cheon.

208
00:24:13,327 --> 00:24:15,829
You're not the president's
Chief of Staff anymore.

209
00:24:16,413 --> 00:24:18,957
This is a completely different world now.

210
00:24:18,958 --> 00:24:20,793
How can you possibly be this clueless?

211
00:24:25,339 --> 00:24:29,218
Baek Kitae has a warrant out
for his arrest.

212
00:24:30,928 --> 00:24:32,720
I warned you, didn't I?

213
00:24:32,721 --> 00:24:36,392
General Hwang isn't the kind of man
who'll go down that easily.

214
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:50,446
That damn bald son of a bitch
is practically invincible, I swear.

215
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:52,491
Oh, stop dwelling on those thoughts.

216
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:56,578
Do you wanna stay here forever?

217
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:04,585
Madam Shin,

218
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:07,213
is there any way for me to be released?

219
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:08,215
Perhaps.

220
00:25:09,842 --> 00:25:12,635
It all depends on how you play this.

221
00:25:12,636 --> 00:25:14,722
This next part is crucial.

222
00:25:17,224 --> 00:25:19,058
Well, look at you!

223
00:25:19,059 --> 00:25:21,060
It's been a while, Chief Cheon.

224
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:26,442
Gosh, you've really been trying
to knock my block off, haven't you?

225
00:25:32,114 --> 00:25:35,575
You should be thanking
Madam Shin right now.

226
00:25:35,576 --> 00:25:38,453
You'd have a bullet in your skull
if it weren't for this woman here,

227
00:25:38,454 --> 00:25:40,122
you son of a bitch.

228
00:25:41,457 --> 00:25:44,918
The truth is, I'm only here
because of her, just so you know.

229
00:25:47,004 --> 00:25:49,381
Anything you wanna share with me?

230
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:52,593
Just talk to him.

231
00:25:53,594 --> 00:25:56,679
I went to a lot of trouble
to arrange this meeting.

232
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:59,433
We need to work together
to find a way to survive.

233
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:01,143
Don't you think?

234
00:26:10,110 --> 00:26:12,821
Apparently he doesn't even
wanna make it through the night.

235
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:15,740
Oh, well.

236
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:17,533
How about this?

237
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:20,286
We'll put you in a shallow grave
alongside Baek Kitae…

238
00:26:23,123 --> 00:26:24,500
The two of you together.

239
00:26:26,794 --> 00:26:29,171
- You piece of garbage!
- General Hwang.

240
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:35,094
What do you want from me, sir?

241
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:40,973
Bang, got ya! Bang, bang!

242
00:26:43,644 --> 00:26:46,188
Now that's the attitude I'm looking for.

243
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:58,199
My fellow citizens,
I'm Cheon Seokjung, Chief of Staff…

244
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:00,369
…to the president.

245
00:27:02,204 --> 00:27:05,540
To begin,
I'd like to express my genuine relief

246
00:27:05,541 --> 00:27:07,416
that the truth has finally come to light.

247
00:27:07,417 --> 00:27:09,711
I'd also like to address
the slush fund ledger,

248
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:13,631
which has been reported on
by many media outlets.

249
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,093
I'd like to be clear.

250
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:20,639
The aforementioned ledger was not mine.

251
00:27:21,557 --> 00:27:25,894
It is the property of KCIA Director
Baek Kitae and documents the scale…

252
00:27:27,646 --> 00:27:29,773
of his elaborate criminal enterprise.

253
00:27:30,774 --> 00:27:34,402
As the Joint Investigation Headquarters
intensified its inquiry

254
00:27:34,403 --> 00:27:36,988
and his crimes
were on the verge of being exposed,

255
00:27:36,989 --> 00:27:39,448
Acting Director Baek Kitae
committed the grave crime

256
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:42,702
of plotting the assassination
of General Hwang Daesik,

257
00:27:42,703 --> 00:27:45,998
the head of the JIH
and a prominent figure in government.

258
00:27:46,623 --> 00:27:50,376
Fortunately, General Hwang
uncovered this violent plot in advance

259
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:52,003
and marshaled a swift response,

260
00:27:52,004 --> 00:27:54,631
foiling the attempt on his life
before it could be carried out.

261
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:15,861
I need you to tell me something.

262
00:28:17,613 --> 00:28:20,699
Why do the reports all say
Cheon's money belongs to Baek Kitae?

263
00:28:22,117 --> 00:28:25,662
I want Cheon close.
He could be useful in the future.

264
00:28:27,456 --> 00:28:29,666
He stepped down as Chief of Staff, so…

265
00:28:33,003 --> 00:28:34,588
Let's wrap this up, all right?

266
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:37,758
You think I struggled for nine years,

267
00:28:38,675 --> 00:28:41,511
surviving through hell on earth,
just to crash and burn like this?

268
00:28:43,931 --> 00:28:47,267
You know damn well Baek Kitae
didn't plan all this on his own.

269
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:52,064
Cheon and Baek Kitae have to go down
together to put a stop to this.

270
00:29:00,822 --> 00:29:02,574
You better be careful.

271
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:08,538
I decide when
and how we end this, Advisor Jang.

272
00:29:09,998 --> 00:29:11,374
Come on, Hwang, wake up!

273
00:29:13,168 --> 00:29:14,628
That's enough, sir. Calm down.

274
00:29:15,796 --> 00:29:17,672
Lower your gun, shithead.

275
00:29:17,673 --> 00:29:18,840
I said that's enough.

276
00:29:35,482 --> 00:29:37,025
Well…

277
00:29:37,818 --> 00:29:39,861
…if it weren't for you, Advisor Jang,

278
00:29:41,613 --> 00:29:43,740
there's no doubt I'd be dead right now.

279
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:50,329
Baek Kitae thought he was so clever.
Thought we'd never see him coming.

280
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:51,957
Sneaky bastard.

281
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:53,834
Hey.

282
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:57,504
You've done an excellent job up until now.

283
00:29:58,088 --> 00:29:59,339
So I think

284
00:30:00,007 --> 00:30:02,008
that you've earned yourself some rest.

285
00:30:02,009 --> 00:30:03,176
What do you say?

286
00:30:27,534 --> 00:30:29,452
I'll send Special Forces with you.

287
00:30:29,453 --> 00:30:31,996
Find Baek and kill him
before the day is over.

288
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:34,374
Yes, sir. I'll put an end to this.

289
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:49,723
Your time's finally up, Baek Kitae.

290
00:30:53,477 --> 00:30:54,769
Breaking news.

291
00:30:54,770 --> 00:30:59,190
The slush fund ledger previously believed
to belong to Chief of Staff Cheon Seokjung

292
00:30:59,191 --> 00:31:04,820
has now been definitively linked
to Acting KCIA Director Baek Kitae.

293
00:31:04,821 --> 00:31:08,449
Earlier this morning,
as the investigation closed in on Baek,

294
00:31:08,450 --> 00:31:10,743
sources say he suddenly disappeared.

295
00:31:10,744 --> 00:31:13,579
Meanwhile, Chief of Staff
Cheon Seokjung has stated that

296
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:17,083
he takes full political responsibility
for the situation

297
00:31:17,084 --> 00:31:19,168
and promptly announced his resignation.

298
00:31:19,169 --> 00:31:21,337
Mr. Cheon also released a public statement

299
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:24,006
calling for a thorough
criminal investigation

300
00:31:24,007 --> 00:31:28,178
into Acting Director Baek Kitae,
who has continued to evade authorities.

301
00:31:45,487 --> 00:31:48,448
Director Baek.
I don't know how they found it,

302
00:31:49,407 --> 00:31:52,201
but the JIH just raided the safe house
in Segeomjeong.

303
00:31:52,202 --> 00:31:55,080
…foiling the attempt on
his life before it could be carried out.

304
00:31:56,456 --> 00:31:57,958
I can say with utmost certainty,

305
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:01,127
- these developments demonstrate…
-  Sir?

306
00:32:01,128 --> 00:32:03,838
…the full extent of Baek Kitae's
traitorous activities.

307
00:32:03,839 --> 00:32:07,341
- His actions will no longer be concealed…
- We can't stay here much longer.

308
00:32:07,342 --> 00:32:10,511
And I would be remiss in my duties
as a former government official…

309
00:32:10,512 --> 00:32:11,887
Where do you wanna go?

310
00:32:11,888 --> 00:32:13,431
…this great nation
if I didn't take a moment

311
00:32:14,266 --> 00:32:18,602
to express my deepest possible gratitude
to General Hwang Daesik,

312
00:32:18,603 --> 00:32:22,439
and call for a thorough and impartial
investigation into Baek Kitae,

313
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,775
who has deceived
the investigative authorities

314
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:27,278
and committed acts of heinous consequence.

315
00:33:08,236 --> 00:33:10,447
So did you finish
what you had to do?

316
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:13,366
I'm sorry.

317
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:15,785
What do you need from me?

318
00:33:17,871 --> 00:33:19,872
Please send a boat for me when you can.

319
00:33:19,873 --> 00:33:21,124
It's an emergency.

320
00:33:22,542 --> 00:33:23,626
All right.

321
00:33:59,246 --> 00:34:00,872
They're sending a boat to Busan.

322
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:02,999
We're headed to Busan then?

323
00:34:06,544 --> 00:34:07,545
How's Kihyun?

324
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,131
Any information?

325
00:34:11,508 --> 00:34:12,842
Not much, sir. Sorry.

326
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:16,429
It appears he was taken
directly to the ER…

327
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:20,100
but that's as much as I've heard.

328
00:34:23,645 --> 00:34:24,646
Just keep checking.

329
00:34:25,772 --> 00:34:26,773
Of course, sir.

330
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,291
What have you got?

331
00:34:45,292 --> 00:34:49,462
Well, my contact in Japan said
Choi Yuji has already left town.

332
00:34:50,046 --> 00:34:54,301
As you suspected he would,
Baek Kitae is probably heading that way.

333
00:34:55,802 --> 00:34:57,429
And Cheon Seokjung?

334
00:34:58,054 --> 00:34:59,431
He's nowhere to be found.

335
00:35:49,522 --> 00:35:51,524
EXPORT IS THE CULMINATION
OF NATIONAL POWER

336
00:35:53,485 --> 00:35:54,486
Kitae.

337
00:35:56,905 --> 00:35:58,031
Wha… What are you…

338
00:36:09,292 --> 00:36:10,377
Look, I know.

339
00:36:12,045 --> 00:36:14,464
I completely understand how you feel.

340
00:36:16,633 --> 00:36:17,926
But I had no choice.

341
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:23,347
Hwang Daesik told me if I didn't obey,
he'd murder me right then and there.

342
00:36:23,348 --> 00:36:25,015
What was I supposed to do?

343
00:36:25,016 --> 00:36:28,395
There are no other moves to make
if you can't even ensure your survival.

344
00:36:31,272 --> 00:36:34,983
If you'd taken care of Hwang Daesik,
we'd be fine by now, Baek.

345
00:36:45,495 --> 00:36:46,830
Just listen, all right?

346
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:51,417
At this point, this country's gonna end up

347
00:36:51,418 --> 00:36:53,461
in the hands of those Army Neanderthals.

348
00:36:56,464 --> 00:36:59,008
We can't be turning on each other
right now.

349
00:37:00,593 --> 00:37:02,721
If I survive, then you survive.

350
00:37:05,306 --> 00:37:06,891
And so does your family.

351
00:37:12,689 --> 00:37:14,733
Hwang and I talked, and we made a deal.

352
00:37:18,027 --> 00:37:20,571
Do some jail time,
just a quick little stint,

353
00:37:20,572 --> 00:37:22,240
and when you come back out…

354
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:26,494
we pick up where we left off
with our business.

355
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:30,665
Just trust me one more time
and we're home free.

356
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:35,920
I'm pretty much the only person
you can trust right now!

357
00:37:39,132 --> 00:37:40,133
What?

358
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:47,557
You think I won't ever get this seat?

359
00:37:54,856 --> 00:37:55,899
Believe me.

360
00:37:57,859 --> 00:37:59,360
Before I die…

361
00:38:02,572 --> 00:38:04,741
you're gonna see
that you're wrong about that.

362
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,833
You deserve to sit here as well.

363
00:38:18,713 --> 00:38:20,215
I've always said that, right?

364
00:38:21,883 --> 00:38:23,218
After me, it's you.

365
00:38:27,013 --> 00:38:28,056
Kitae.

366
00:38:32,393 --> 00:38:34,145
We have more cards left in the deck.

367
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:38,191
What happened to trust?

368
00:38:44,781 --> 00:38:48,243
Have you ever trusted me?

369
00:38:57,877 --> 00:38:59,420
That's what I thought.

370
00:40:22,545 --> 00:40:23,629
Ugh, goddamn it.

371
00:40:39,395 --> 00:40:41,064
Where were you? I-I, uh…

372
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:46,444
I was just trying to clear things out.

373
00:40:48,071 --> 00:40:51,324
50, 71, 16.

374
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:55,703
Open it.

375
00:40:59,332 --> 00:41:00,583
What's the combo?

376
00:41:01,584 --> 00:41:03,336
Shit, it's hot.

377
00:41:10,718 --> 00:41:12,095
Seventy-one.

378
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:17,225
- Sixteen.
- Sixteen.

379
00:41:38,413 --> 00:41:40,163
This is everything?

380
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:42,834
What's wrong? Not enough?

381
00:41:44,502 --> 00:41:47,963
I just expected a lot more than this.

382
00:41:49,298 --> 00:41:50,550
Oh, shit.

383
00:41:54,429 --> 00:41:57,223
Where did I leave it now?

384
00:41:58,391 --> 00:41:59,975
Give me a break, man.

385
00:42:02,770 --> 00:42:03,771
Well…

386
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:13,364
After you failed to take out Hwang,

387
00:42:14,073 --> 00:42:15,658
they turned off the power here.

388
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:18,327
Turned off all utilities.

389
00:42:20,163 --> 00:42:21,581
Water, too.

390
00:42:34,927 --> 00:42:37,013
Shame, isn't it?

391
00:42:37,597 --> 00:42:40,975
You did all the hard work,
and someone else got rich.

392
00:42:42,602 --> 00:42:45,646
Cheon Seokjung took it for himself
and hung you out to dry.

393
00:42:56,199 --> 00:42:57,200
Kitae.

394
00:43:01,954 --> 00:43:04,832
You and I… are humble servants.

395
00:43:05,792 --> 00:43:08,878
Government lackeys. Right?

396
00:43:12,048 --> 00:43:14,467
We just try our best
to do what we're told.

397
00:43:15,468 --> 00:43:17,178
We're both resigned to that fate.

398
00:43:18,971 --> 00:43:20,723
Come on, how much power do we have?

399
00:43:22,767 --> 00:43:25,561
Is that why you jumped into bed
with Jang again, you bald little rat?

400
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:30,066
It's not what you think, okay?

401
00:43:31,150 --> 00:43:32,193
I'll explain it.

402
00:43:34,862 --> 00:43:36,071
Just listen…

403
00:44:01,222 --> 00:44:02,223
Kitae.

404
00:44:13,234 --> 00:44:14,402
Don't do this.

405
00:44:16,112 --> 00:44:17,738
I'll do anything you want.

406
00:44:18,948 --> 00:44:20,116
I swear!

407
00:44:20,741 --> 00:44:22,493
I won't ever betray you again.

408
00:44:23,452 --> 00:44:25,621
I'll help you get
everything you ever wanted!

409
00:44:27,081 --> 00:44:28,499
I swear to God.

410
00:44:46,392 --> 00:44:47,518
Kitae.

411
00:44:48,895 --> 00:44:50,021
Kitae!

412
00:44:52,607 --> 00:44:53,608
Listen.

413
00:44:55,109 --> 00:44:58,362
I told Jang everything.
It's all true, okay?

414
00:44:59,030 --> 00:45:02,116
You're right, I told him everything.
Happy now?

415
00:45:04,327 --> 00:45:07,413
I know you murdered Director General Hwang
and took his seat.

416
00:45:09,248 --> 00:45:10,249
So, hey.

417
00:45:11,209 --> 00:45:12,668
How are we different, huh?

418
00:45:15,922 --> 00:45:17,089
Huh?

419
00:45:19,634 --> 00:45:21,802
Why am I the one who has to die?

420
00:45:24,680 --> 00:45:26,724
Why me? Huh? Why?

421
00:45:27,808 --> 00:45:29,518
Why am I the only one?

422
00:45:30,895 --> 00:45:34,190
Hey! Why am I the one who has to die?

423
00:46:07,473 --> 00:46:09,850
The boat should be arriving
in three hours, sir.

424
00:46:13,688 --> 00:46:15,523
We need to leave for Busan right away.

425
00:46:17,358 --> 00:46:18,526
And Kihyun?

426
00:46:22,446 --> 00:46:23,572
Well, sir…

427
00:46:24,198 --> 00:46:25,408
Tell me.

428
00:46:27,034 --> 00:46:28,619
Apparently he's in bad shape.

429
00:46:54,645 --> 00:46:56,022
Baek Kihyun. How is he?

430
00:46:57,440 --> 00:46:58,441
They said…

431
00:47:00,067 --> 00:47:01,485
he might not make it much longer.

432
00:47:30,014 --> 00:47:32,016
SEONGSAN HOSPITAL

433
00:49:16,245 --> 00:49:18,414
208 - BAEK KIHYUN

434
00:50:15,971 --> 00:50:18,140
SEONGSAN HOSPITAL

435
00:59:28,857 --> 00:59:30,734
You still think you're in the right?

436
00:59:32,110 --> 00:59:33,653
Are you that stupid and naive?

437
00:59:39,159 --> 00:59:41,870
You think by taking me down,
you're changing the world?

438
00:59:44,706 --> 00:59:46,166
I guess you still don't get it.

439
00:59:49,169 --> 00:59:50,504
The world has already changed.

440
00:59:53,548 --> 00:59:54,966
And the thing is…

441
00:59:57,344 --> 00:59:59,346
there isn't a place for you in it.

442
01:00:04,309 --> 01:00:05,477
You're finished.

443
01:00:10,941 --> 01:00:11,942
What about you?

444
01:00:14,653 --> 01:00:16,029
Where do you fit?

445
01:03:01,945 --> 01:03:03,071
I was…

446
01:03:04,572 --> 01:03:05,907
serving my country.

447
01:03:08,159 --> 01:03:09,661
Everything I did…

448
01:03:11,830 --> 01:03:14,081
I did for the sake of this nation.

449
01:04:16,144 --> 01:04:17,686
Mommy?

450
01:04:22,192 --> 01:04:23,610
Are you okay?

451
01:04:24,986 --> 01:04:26,321
Here, sweetie.

452
01:04:29,491 --> 01:04:31,659
I'm okay.

453
01:04:33,036 --> 01:04:34,412
Mommy's okay.

454
01:04:36,414 --> 01:04:37,540
Everything's okay.

455
01:05:20,792 --> 01:05:22,835
All I can say is, "Good riddance."

456
01:05:32,470 --> 01:05:34,304
Ah, look who it is.

457
01:05:34,305 --> 01:05:36,015
So, are you leaving town?

458
01:05:43,565 --> 01:05:45,066
Thanks for your hard work.

459
01:05:46,693 --> 01:05:48,278
Where's the 70 billion?

460
01:05:49,404 --> 01:05:51,363
Where'd you put all that money?

461
01:05:53,032 --> 01:05:55,117
Uh-oh, here we go.

462
01:05:55,118 --> 01:05:57,494
I told you, it's going right
into the country's treasury.

463
01:05:57,495 --> 01:05:58,829
Can you believe this?

464
01:06:02,292 --> 01:06:05,252
Ah, man, look at this guy.

465
01:06:05,253 --> 01:06:07,130
- All right, Colonel Ahn. Got it?
- Yes, sir.

466
01:06:09,215 --> 01:06:10,925
Geez, what a mess, huh?

467
01:06:17,056 --> 01:06:18,850
And what's this?

468
01:06:19,517 --> 01:06:21,185
A token of my gratitude.

469
01:06:21,186 --> 01:06:24,021
Shame to watch you walk around
in that shabby wardrobe

470
01:06:24,022 --> 01:06:25,190
for the rest of your life.

471
01:06:25,982 --> 01:06:29,359
You're a man who's supposed to be
serving his country, after all.

472
01:06:29,360 --> 01:06:31,445
If you're gonna
become a high-power prosecutor

473
01:06:31,446 --> 01:06:32,738
or a bigwig attorney,

474
01:06:32,739 --> 01:06:35,450
you'll need one good suit,
won't you?

475
01:06:36,868 --> 01:06:39,412
Oh, gosh. Well…

476
01:07:22,997 --> 01:07:24,207
You going back?

477
01:07:25,333 --> 01:07:26,668
To Busan, I mean?

478
01:07:28,002 --> 01:07:29,003
Yes.

479
01:07:30,463 --> 01:07:33,424
And what about you? What's your next move?

480
01:08:20,555 --> 01:08:21,806
Excuse me, Colonel Baek?

481
01:08:26,853 --> 01:08:28,104
You have any regrets?

482
01:08:31,733 --> 01:08:33,943
You have to kill Baek Kitae.

483
01:08:36,821 --> 01:08:39,532
That's the only way
you'll survive this now.

484
01:08:41,868 --> 01:08:45,872
And the same goes for your sister
and your little niece.

485
01:08:48,291 --> 01:08:50,376
It's the only way they'll live.

486
01:09:31,292 --> 01:09:34,212
I remember saying something
a while back to Baek Kitae.

487
01:09:35,088 --> 01:09:36,338
Something like…

488
01:09:36,339 --> 01:09:39,800
"Claiming you acted the way you did
because the world is crazy

489
01:09:39,801 --> 01:09:41,761
is nothing more than a flimsy excuse."

490
01:09:43,471 --> 01:09:45,305
At the end of the day,

491
01:09:45,306 --> 01:09:48,017
everyone makes their own choices
in this life.

492
01:09:49,936 --> 01:09:51,104
As for me?

493
01:09:52,063 --> 01:09:53,898
In order to bring him down,

494
01:09:54,649 --> 01:09:56,233
I sold out.

495
01:09:56,234 --> 01:09:59,737
I gave up my own sense of duty
and patriotism to the men in power.

496
01:10:00,947 --> 01:10:02,407
Baek Kitae and I…

497
01:10:04,701 --> 01:10:06,327
both betrayed our values.

498
01:10:09,080 --> 01:10:11,040
And what was it all really for?

499
01:10:18,297 --> 01:10:20,049
-  My friend.
-  Yes, sir.

500
01:10:21,175 --> 01:10:23,886
Keep a close watch on Cho
and report to me regularly.

501
01:10:24,470 --> 01:10:25,971
Of course, sir.

502
01:10:25,972 --> 01:10:29,141
I think it's time to go in, Madam Shin.

503
01:10:29,142 --> 01:10:30,852
'Cause I'm getting impatient.

504
01:10:31,853 --> 01:10:33,062
All right, let's go.

505
01:10:54,709 --> 01:10:56,711
So, I'll be the director?

506
01:12:29,887 --> 01:12:31,180
My friend.
